course: dictionary
lesson: 6728
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one the writer means. An ointment is a smooth, greasy cream rubbed on the skin to heal cuts, burns, rashes or sore places. If a nurse says, "Put a little ointment on that cut," the clue is the cut, so the word means the cream.
explain: The word has a second meaning, used in church and Bible stories. There, ointment is oil or perfumed oil used for anointing. You would only know this meaning from the story around it, such as a woman pouring precious ointment on someone's head.
explain: Look at the example sentence: Father William tries to sell his son «an ointment at one shilling the box». Selling and the price are the clues. Here an ointment is something you buy in a shop, and the silly story is part of the joke. Always check: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Ointment also appears in a saying: «a fly in the ointment» means one small thing that spoils something good. A lovely day at the beach could have one fly in the ointment, such as a sudden shower. An idiom does not mean what its words say, so the context is your guide.
fact: An ointment is a smooth, greasy cream rubbed on the skin.
fact: Ointments can heal cuts, burns, rashes and sore places.
fact: «An ointment at one shilling the box» means a cream sold for a price, and a shilling was an old British coin.
fact: «A fly in the ointment» means one small thing that spoils something good.
fact: Only use medicine or ointment that an adult gives you, because medicines can harm you if used wrongly.
exercise: The nurse said, «Put a little ointment on that cut.» What is an ointment? | *A smooth, greasy cream for healing skin | A sharp tool for cutting cloth | A loud drum used in a band
exercise: In «an ointment at one shilling the box», what is being sold? | A bicycle | *An ointment | A pair of shoes | A ticket to a show
exercise: What does «a fly in the ointment» mean? | A cure for flies | A bug stuck in some cream | *One small thing that spoils something good | A very large insect
test: In a church story, a woman pours precious ointment on someone's head. What kind of ointment is it? | A cream for sunburn | *Oil or perfumed oil used for anointing | A type of bread | A cold drink
test: Why should you only use medicine or ointment that an adult gives you? | It tastes nice | It is always sweet | *Medicines can harm you if used wrongly | It makes you taller
exam: Which is the best meaning of ointment in «Father William tries to sell his son an ointment»? | A loud drum | A spoken promise | *A greasy cream you can buy | A small fish | A type of shoe
